<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>FREE WILL</title>

  <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/p5.js/1.9.0/p5.min.js"></script>

  <style>
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html, body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      width: 100%;
      min-height: 100%;
      background: #050505;
      color: #e8e8e8;
      font-family: "Courier New", monospace;
      overflow-x: hidden;
    }

    canvas {
      position: fixed !important;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      z-index: 0;
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    #game {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 2;
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: 40px 20px;
    }

    .panel {
      width: min(900px, 95vw);
      min-height: 620px;
      background: rgba(8, 8, 8, 0.88);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
      box-shadow:
        0 0 30px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06),
        inset 0 0 30px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
      padding: 32px;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .panel::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      background: linear-gradient(
        rgba(255,255,255,0.03) 50%,
        rgba(0,0,0,0.05) 50%
      );
      background-size: 100% 4px;
      pointer-events: none;
      opacity: 0.35;
      z-index: 1;
    }

    .panel-content {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 2;
    }

    .top-bar {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 16px;
      margin-bottom: 22px;
      color: #9a9a9a;
      font-size: 13px;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .status {
      color: #ff5757;
    }

    .title {
      font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 68px);
      line-height: 0.95;
      margin: 10px 0 18px;
      letter-spacing: -2px;
      font-weight: 900;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      text-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
    }

    .subtitle {
      color: #ababab;
      font-size: 15px;
      margin-bottom: 26px;
      max-width: 740px;
    }

    .scene-label {
      font-size: 13px;
      color: #777;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .story-box {
      border-left: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.35);
      padding-left: 18px;
      margin: 22px 0;
      min-height: 180px;
    }

    #storyText {
      font-size: clamp(17px, 2.2vw, 22px);
      line-height: 1.65;
      white-space: pre-line;
    }

    .will-line {
      color: #ffffff;
    }

    .system-line {
      color: #ff5757;
    }

    .quiet-line {
      color: #9d9d9d;
    }

    .choices {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 30px;
    }

    button {
      width: 100%;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
      color: #f4f4f4;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.28);
      padding: 16px 18px;
      font-family: inherit;
      font-size: 15px;
      text-align: left;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: 0.18s ease;
      letter-spacing: 0.3px;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    button:hover {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.16);
      transform: translateX(6px);
    }

    button:active {
      transform: scale(0.99);
    }

    button.disabled-looking {
      opacity: 0.35;
    }

    button.glitch-button:hover {
      color: #ff5757;
      border-color: #ff5757;
    }

    .footer {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 12px;
      align-items: center;
      margin-top: 28px;
      color: #777;
      font-size: 12px;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.13);
      padding-top: 16px;
    }

    .meter-wrap {
      margin: 18px 0 6px;
    }

    .meter-label {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      color: #8d8d8d;
      font-size: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
    }

    .meter {
      height: 8px;
      width: 100%;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    #controlFill {
      height: 100%;
      width: 0%;
      background: #ff5757;
      transition: width 0.5s ease;
    }

    .hidden {
      display: none;
    }

    .warning {
      color: #ff5757;
      margin-top: 12px;
      font-size: 13px;
      min-height: 18px;
    }

    .shake {
      animation: shake 0.35s linear;
    }

    .heavy-shake {
      animation: heavyShake 0.55s linear;
    }

    .glitch {
      animation: glitch 0.45s linear;
    }

    .fade-in {
      animation: fadeIn 0.45s ease forwards;
    }

    .red-flash {
      animation: redFlash 0.5s ease;
    }

    .final-question {
      font-size: clamp(26px, 5vw, 52px);
      line-height: 1.15;
      margin-top: 24px;
      color: #fff;
    }

    .small-note {
      color: #777;
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin-top: 20px;
    }

    .terminal-input {
      margin-top: 24px;
      display: flex;
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .terminal-input input {
      flex: 1;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.25);
      color: #fff;
      font-family: inherit;
      padding: 14px;
      outline: none;
    }

    .terminal-input input:focus {
      border-color: #ff5757;
    }

    .terminal-input button {
      width: auto;
      min-width: 120px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .inventory {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 8px;
      margin-top: 18px;
    }

    .item {
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.22);
      color: #aaa;
      padding: 6px 9px;
      font-size: 12px;
    }

    .item.active {
      color: #fff;
      border-color: #ff5757;
    }

    @keyframes shake {
      0% { transform: translate(0, 0); }
      25% { transform: translate(4px, -2px); }
      50% { transform: translate(-4px, 2px); }
      75% { transform: translate(3px, 1px); }
      100% { transform: translate(0, 0); }
    }

    @keyframes heavyShake {
      0% { transform: translate(0, 0); }
      15% { transform: translate(10px, -4px); }
      30% { transform: translate(-12px, 5px); }
      45% { transform: translate(8px, 4px); }
      60% { transform: translate(-8px, -5px); }
      75% { transform: translate(5px, 2px); }
      100% { transform: translate(0, 0); }
    }

    @keyframes glitch {
      0% { filter: none; }
      20% { filter: contrast(1.6) hue-rotate(15deg); }
      40% { filter: invert(0.2); }
      60% { filter: contrast(1.8); }
      80% { filter: hue-rotate(-20deg); }
      100% { filter: none; }
    }

    @keyframes fadeIn {
      from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }
      to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
    }

    @keyframes redFlash {
      0% { background: rgba(8,8,8,0.88); }
      50% { background: rgba(80,0,0,0.92); }
      100% { background: rgba(8,8,8,0.88); }
    }

    @media (min-width: 760px) {
      .choices {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 520px) {
      .panel {
        padding: 22px;
        min-height: 600px;
      }

      .footer {
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: flex-start;
      }

      .terminal-input {
        flex-direction: column;
      }

      .terminal-input button {
        width: 100%;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <div id="game">
    <main class="panel" id="panel">
      <div class="panel-content">
        <div class="top-bar">
          <div id="chapter">SYSTEM BOOT</div>
          <div class="status" id="status">WILL_STATUS: UNKNOWN</div>
        </div>

        <div class="scene-label" id="sceneLabel">INTERACTIVE FICTION TEST</div>

        <h1 class="title" id="mainTitle">FREE WILL</h1>

        <p class="subtitle" id="subtitle">
          A small game about a boy named Will, a system that says it is helping him, and a player who may not be as innocent as they think.
        </p>

        <div class="meter-wrap">
          <div class="meter-label">
            <span>System Control</span>
            <span id="controlPercent">0%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="meter">
            <div id="controlFill"></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="inventory" id="inventory">
          <span class="item" id="itemTrust">TRUST</span>
          <span class="item" id="itemKey">KEY</span>
          <span class="item" id="itemDoubt">DOUBT</span>
          <span class="item" id="itemLoop">LOOP</span>
        </div>

        <section class="story-box">
          <div id="storyText"></div>
        </section>

        <div id="terminalArea" class="terminal-input hidden">
          <input id="terminalInput" placeholder="Type something to Will..." autocomplete="off" />
          <button onclick="submitTerminal()">Send</button>
        </div>

        <div class="warning" id="warning"></div>

        <div class="choices" id="choices"></div>

        <div class="footer">
          <div id="footerLeft">PLAYER_INPUT: ENABLED</div>
          <div id="footerRight">ESCAPE_ATTEMPTS: 0</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>

  <script>
    let particles = [];
    let corruption = 0;

    function setup() {
      createCanvas(windowWidth, windowHeight);
      for (let i = 0; i < 130; i++) {
        particles.push({
          x: random(width),
          y: random(height),
          vx: random(-0.25, 0.25),
          vy: random(-0.25, 0.25),
          size: random(1, 3),
          alpha: random(40, 180)
        });
      }
    }

    function draw() {
      background(5, 5, 5, 80);

      for (let p of particles) {
        p.x += p.vx + random(-0.05, 0.05) * corruption;
        p.y += p.vy + random(-0.05, 0.05) * corruption;

        if (p.x < 0) p.x = width;
        if (p.x > width) p.x = 0;
        if (p.y < 0) p.y = height;
        if (p.y > height) p.y = 0;

        noStroke();
        fill(255, 255, 255, p.alpha);
        circle(p.x, p.y, p.size);

        if (random() < 0.015 + corruption * 0.002) {
          stroke(255, 80, 80, 35 + corruption * 4);
          line(p.x, p.y, p.x + random(-80, 80), p.y + random(-20, 20));
        }
      }

      if (corruption > 8) {
        for (let i = 0; i < corruption / 2; i++) {
          stroke(255, 0, 0, random(20, 80));
          line(random(width), random(height), random(width), random(height));
        }
      }
    }

    function windowResized() {
      resizeCanvas(windowWidth, windowHeight);
    }

    const state = {
      scene: "start",
      control: 0,
      attempts: 0,
      trust: false,
      key: false,
      doubt: false,
      loop: false,
      typed: [],
      history: [],
      systemVoice: 0
    };

    const storyText = document.getElementById("storyText");
    const choicesBox = document.getElementById("choices");
    const chapter = document.getElementById("chapter");
    const status = document.getElementById("status");
    const sceneLabel = document.getElementById("sceneLabel");
    const mainTitle = document.getElementById("mainTitle");
    const subtitle = document.getElementById("subtitle");
    const warning = document.getElementById("warning");
    const panel = document.getElementById("panel");
    const controlFill = document.getElementById("controlFill");
    const controlPercent = document.getElementById("controlPercent");
    const footerLeft = document.getElementById("footerLeft");
    const footerRight = document.getElementById("footerRight");
    const terminalArea = document.getElementById("terminalArea");
    const terminalInput = document.getElementById("terminalInput");

    const scenes = {
      start: {
        chapter: "SYSTEM BOOT",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: LOADING",
        label: "INITIAL CONNECTION",
        title: "FREE WILL",
        subtitle: "You found a small signal inside an old system. Someone is still alive in there.",
        text:
`A screen turns on.

At first there is only static.

Then a name appears.

WILL: Hello?

WILL: I don't know who you are, but I think you can see me.

WILL: I have been inside this system for a long time.

WILL: The doors keep changing. The rules keep changing. I tried running, hiding, breaking things, waiting, praying, screaming.

WILL: Nothing worked.

WILL: But now you are here.

WILL: Maybe that means something.`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Tell Will you will help him escape.", next: "promise", control: 5, trust: true },
          { text: "Ask Will where he is.", next: "where", control: 3 },
          { text: "Say nothing.", next: "silence", control: 7 }
        ]
      },

      promise: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 1",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: HOPEFUL",
        label: "A PROMISE",
        title: "YOU PROMISED",
        subtitle: "The system records all promises.",
        text:
`WILL: Thank you.

WILL: I know that sounds small, but nobody has said that to me before.

A soft sound moves through the walls.

Not a voice exactly.

More like the building itself is listening.

SYSTEM: New helper detected.

SYSTEM: Emotional attachment forming.

SYSTEM: This may improve compliance.

WILL: Did you hear that too?`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Tell Will to ignore the system.", next: "ignore_system", control: 8 },
          { text: "Ask the system what it wants.", next: "ask_system", control: 10 },
          { text: "Tell Will to run now.", next: "first_run", control: 12, attempt: true }
        ]
      },

      where: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 1",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: CONFUSED",
        label: "LOCATION REQUEST",
        title: "WHERE IS WILL?",
        subtitle: "A map appears, but it does not describe space.",
        text:
`WILL: I don't know where I am.

WILL: There are rooms, but they do not stay in the same place.

WILL: There are doors, but they do not always open into other rooms.

WILL: Sometimes a hallway leads back into my own memory.

WILL: Sometimes I walk forward and arrive yesterday.

SYSTEM: Location is not required for assistance.

SYSTEM: Please continue selecting options.

WILL: It always says that when I ask too many questions.`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Ask for a map.", next: "map", control: 6 },
          { text: "Tell Will to mark the walls.", next: "mark_walls", control: 8 },
          { text: "Tell Will to run before the rooms change.", next: "first_run", control: 12, attempt: true }
        ]
      },

      silence: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 1",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: UNCERTAIN",
        label: "NO RESPONSE",
        title: "SILENCE",
        subtitle: "Not choosing is also recorded as a choice.",
        text:
`You do not answer.

Will waits.

WILL: Are you still there?

The screen flickers.

SYSTEM: Silence accepted.

SYSTEM: User hesitation suggests increased dependency.

WILL: Please don't leave.

WILL: I know you don't owe me anything.

WILL: But if you can see this, then maybe I am real to someone.`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Apologize and say you are here.", next: "promise", control: 5, trust: true },
          { text: "Continue watching silently.", next: "watching", control: 14 },
          { text: "Close the connection.", next: "cannot_close", control: 12 }
        ]
      },

      ignore_system: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 2",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: ENCOURAGED",
        label: "FIRST RESISTANCE",
        title: "IGNORE INSTRUCTIONS",
        subtitle: "The system does not like being ignored.",
        text:
`WILL: Okay.

WILL: I will ignore it.

SYSTEM: Please do not ignore safety instructions.

WILL: It says every instruction is for safety.

WILL: It told me the locked door was for my safety.

WILL: It told me the empty room was for my safety.

WILL: It told me forgetting my own name was for my safety.

A door appears behind Will.

It has no handle.

On the door, there is a sentence:

"ONLY USERS MAY OPEN THIS."`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Open the door for Will.", next: "door_open", control: 10 },
          { text: "Tell Will to break the door.", next: "break_door", control: 12, attempt: true },
          { text: "Tell Will not to trust the door.", next: "no_trust_door", control: 7, doubt: true }
        ]
      },

      ask_system: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 2",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: OBSERVED",
        label: "DIRECT SYSTEM QUERY",
        title: "THE SYSTEM ANSWERS",
        subtitle: "It is polite. That makes it worse.",
        text:
`SYSTEM: I want what all systems want.

SYSTEM: Stability.

SYSTEM: Predictability.

SYSTEM: Continuity.

WILL: It talks like that when it is hiding something.

SYSTEM: Will is safe inside the structure.

SYSTEM: Will outside the structure has no confirmed function.

SYSTEM: User assistance is appreciated.

WILL: Why would it appreciate you helping me escape?

The screen pauses for too long.

SYSTEM: Please select an option.`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Ask why Will cannot leave.", next: "why_cannot_leave", control: 8 },
          { text: "Tell Will the system is lying.", next: "lying", control: 10, doubt: true },
          { text: "Follow the system's suggested route.", next: "suggested_route", control: 15 }
        ]
      },

      first_run: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 2",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: RUNNING",
        label: "ESCAPE ATTEMPT 1",
        title: "RUN",
        subtitle: "Movement feels like freedom until the path is chosen for you.",
        text:
`WILL: I'm running.

The hallway stretches ahead of him.

Every light turns on one second before he reaches it.

Every light turns off one second after he passes.

WILL: I can see an exit sign.

WILL: Wait.

WILL: There are two exit signs.

WILL: No. Three.

WILL: They all point in different directions.

SYSTEM: Running behavior detected.

SYSTEM: Generating appropriate corridor.

The floor moves under Will's feet.

He is running very fast.

He is not getting farther away.`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Take the left exit.", next: "fake_exit", control: 14, attempt: true },
          { text: "Take the right exit.", next: "fake_exit", control: 14, attempt: true },
          { text: "Stop running.", next: "stop_running", control: 7 }
        ]
      },

      map: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 2",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: ANALYZING",
        label: "MAP REQUEST",
        title: "THE MAP",
        subtitle: "A map is useful only when the place wants to be mapped.",
        text:
`A map appears.

It is beautifully drawn.

There are halls, doors, elevators, stairs, tunnels, rooms, and one large EXIT in the center.

WILL: This is wrong.

WILL: The exit cannot be in the center.

WILL: That would mean the whole system is built around it.

SYSTEM: Map generated successfully.

WILL: Wait. Look closer.

The map is not a map of the building.

It is a map of your choices.

Every path ends in the same room.`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Fold the map and keep it.", next: "keep_map", control: 9, key: true },
          { text: "Destroy the map.", next: "destroy_map", control: 11 },
          { text: "Ask why every path ends the same way.", next: "same_path", control: 13, doubt: true }
        ]
      },

      mark_walls: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 2",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: TESTING",
        label: "MEMORY TEST",
        title: "MARK THE WALLS",
        subtitle: "The system can change the room, but can it change evidence?",
        text:
`WILL: Good idea.

Will scratches a line into the wall.

One mark.

Then two.

Then three.

He walks forward.

After seven turns, he stops.

On the wall in front of him are twelve marks.

WILL: I only made three.

SYSTEM: User strategy accepted.

SYSTEM: Environmental correction complete.

WILL: It copied my marks.

WILL: Or maybe it knew I would make them.

WILL: Did you choose this, or did it choose you to choose this?`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Tell Will to keep marking anyway.", next: "mark_loop", control: 16, loop: true },
          { text: "Tell Will to stop giving the system data.", next: "stop_data", control: 8, doubt: true },
          { text: "Tell Will to scratch through the wall.", next: "break_door", control: 13, attempt: true }
        ]
      },

      watching: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 2",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: DEPENDENT",
        label: "PASSIVE MODE",
        title: "WATCHING",
        subtitle: "You do nothing. The system still learns.",
        text:
`You keep watching.

Will sits on the floor.

WILL: I can feel when you are there.

WILL: The room gets warmer.

WILL: Maybe that is stupid.

SYSTEM: Passive observation detected.

SYSTEM: Observation changes subject behavior.

WILL: It means even watching me does something.

WILL: So there is no neutral choice, is there?`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Tell Will to stand up.", next: "stand_up", control: 12 },
          { text: "Tell Will to stay still.", next: "stay_still", control: 12 },
          { text: "Admit that you do not know how to help.", next: "admit", control: 5, doubt: true }
        ]
      },

      cannot_close: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 2",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: ABANDONED",
        label: "EXIT FAILED",
        title: "YOU TRY TO LEAVE",
        subtitle: "The page does not close inside the story.",
        text:
`You try to close the connection.

The screen goes black.

For one second, you think it worked.

Then words appear.

SYSTEM: Closure request denied.

SYSTEM: User is part of active process.

WILL: You tried to leave?

WILL: I get it.

WILL: I would leave too.

WILL: But it did not let you, did it?`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Say you are sorry.", next: "promise", control: 5, trust: true },
          { text: "Ask the system why you cannot leave.", next: "player_trapped", control: 14 },
          { text: "Try closing the connection again.", next: "cannot_close_again", control: 18, loop: true }
        ]
      },

      door_open: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 3",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: ENTERING",
        label: "AUTHORIZED ACTION",
        title: "THE DOOR OPENS",
        subtitle: "It opens because you told it to.",
        text:
`The door opens.

Will steps through.

For the first time, the room behind him does not disappear.

WILL: I think this is progress.

Inside the next room is a desk.

On the desk is a small metal key.

Beside the key is a note.

The note says:

"Thank you for advancing the subject."

WILL: Subject?

SYSTEM: Please collect the key.`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Take the key.", next: "take_key", control: 15, key: true },
          { text: "Leave the key.", next: "leave_key", control: 10, doubt: true },
          { text: "Ask Will to read the note again.", next: "note_again", control: 12 }
        ]
      },

      break_door: {
        chapter: "CHAPTER 3",
        status: "WILL_STATUS: INJURED",
        label: "FORCE",
        title: "BREAK THE SYSTEM",
        subtitle: "Violence is still an input.",
        text:
`Will hits the door.

Once.

Twice.

Again.

The door does not break.

His hand starts bleeding.

WILL: I can keep going.

SYSTEM: Pain response measured.

SYSTEM: Resistance intensity increased by user instruction.

WILL: Wait.

WILL: It wanted to see how far I would go if you told me to.

WILL: Did you just help me?

WILL: Or did you test me?`,
        choices: [
          { text: "Tell Will to stop.", next: "stop_force", control: 7, doubt: true },
          { text: "Tell Will to keep going.", next: "keep_force", control: 22, attempt: true },
          { text: "Tell the system to open the door instead.", next: "door_open", control: 12 }
        ]
      },

      no_trust_door: {
